{"kind":"report","text":"Approved DESIGN planning baseline at exactc57e08207dc9ab5aa415bad3bf6f645cd5b856f2/tree2b855e7b55e34a87a7e7a936e5123a6a7ecfa876, sole primary artifact86c6c448, complete452line note read. Binds design-note requesta1889c73/promise39439c9d only.\n\nArchitecture conclusion: approved. The room model starts from work, source and decisions/outcomes without forcing storage concepts or new navigation tabs. All8required contracts are coherent: exact identity/context; typed edges/provenance; bounded authorized lookup/search/aggregation; coherent multi-head captured views/coverage; versioned source/compare; offered action and durable custody; host-owned app projections/trust; execution evidence/external outcomes. Source inventory correctly separates public/current, internal-only and missing capability. Directory fixed repository/branch, one-file versus tree manifests, selected accept-report facts, job subject/configuration versus actual checker authority, partial Git helpers, bounded metadata versus unbounded signer preparation, Page enumeration/text failure distinctions and missing production runner are supported by40e37d source. No atomic room snapshot, universal graph API, general deployment runner or arbitrary repository access is inferred.\n\nSecurity conclusion: approved at design-boundary scope. Authority precedes existence/counts, including bounded eligibility/index migration; source publication access is separated from member exploration. Missing/stale/denied/unavailable/redacted/unsupported and incomplete coverage cannot silently become absence or completion. Routes contain nonsecret context while actor/draft authority remains bound internally. Exact requests/results and unknown mutations retain custody semantics. Generic views cannot run package code merely to interpret data; unfamiliar applications keep safe generic homes without fabricated forge meanings. Adopted application isolation, separate semantic/presentation/release identities and archive privacy/credential-safe history obligations remain separate, with no exception granted.\n\nSimplification conclusion: approved. One canonical home per fact, a connected ordinary journey first, stable navigation/Back, focused expansion and equivalent structured lists keep complexity tied to a user's question. Specialized diagrams must improve a named task against direct-list baselines. Mobile destinations, keyboard/screen-reader equivalence, focus/touch/zoom/reflow/reduced-motion checks are acceptance conditions, not claimed completed testing. No framework/shell replacement or premature graph UI is commissioned.\n\nVisualization integrity: Tufte review accepts explicit units/populations/grouping/deduplication/head selection and literal-contributor drilldown. Pairwise incidence counts are separated from distinct entities; unequal totals/duplicate entities must be disclosed, and a multi-edge association cannot manufacture attributed goal-to-file tuples. Unlinked work remains visible. Overlap is separated from text conflict/extent relation; ancestry and temporal order do not become business dependency/causality; no unsupported progress/critical-path metric. There is no rendered numerical chart here on which to calculate a lie factor or certify scale/layout usability. The follow-up contract/study must choose encodings and thresholds before claiming those results.\n\nPrimary references checked support the limited rationale: Tower full historic tree https://www.git-tower.com/help/guides/commit-history/historic-file-trees/mac ; GitLab snapshot versus merge-base comparisons https://docs.gitlab.com/user/project/repository/compare_revisions/ ; numeric ribbon widths/acyclic D3 https://github.com/d3/d3-sankey ; categorical Parallel Sets https://eagereyes.org/publications/Kosara-TVCG-2006 ; task-dependent graph/matrix comparison https://mohammad.ghoniem.info/research/ivs-usability-2005.pdf ; focused context expansion https://dig.cmu.edu/publications/2009-doigraphs.html ; U